# Structure

> The physical shape of the repository. A new top-level folder is an
> architecture change, not a convenience.

## 1. Tree

```text
{{TREE}}
```

- `{{SOURCE_DIR}}` — production source.
- `{{TEST_LOCATION}}` — tests.
- `docs/planning/` — foundation documents and diagrams (hand written).
- `docs/harness/` — how the harness works (hand written).
- `{{GENERATED_DOCS}}` — generated documentation (build output, never edited).
- `scripts/` — harness and tooling.
- `BACKLOG.md` — user stories.

## 2. What lives where

| Folder          | Holds                          | Does not hold       |
| --------------- | ------------------------------ | ------------------- |
| {{FEATURE_DIR}} | one feature, with its tests    | shared utilities    |
| {{SHARED_DIR}}  | reusable, dependency-free code | I/O, feature state  |
| {{CORE_DIR}}    | services and the I/O boundary  | UI code             |
| {{MODELS_DIR}}  | pure types and schemas         | runtime behavior    |

## 3. Naming

| Element       | Convention      | Example            |
| ------------- | --------------- | ------------------ |
| File          | kebab-case      | `auth-service.ts`  |
| Type/class    | PascalCase      | `AuthService`      |
| Function      | camelCase       | `issueToken()`     |
| Test          | colocated spec  | `auth-service.spec.ts` |

## 4. Dependency direction

```text
feature → shared → core → models
```

- No cycles.
- `shared` never imports a feature.
- `models` imports nothing from I/O or UI.
- Cross-package imports require an explicit export.

## 5. Generated documentation

- Path: `{{GENERATED_DOCS}}`.
- Produced by: {{DOC_GENERATOR}}.
- Never edited by hand; never committed unless the project explicitly tracks it.
- The source of truth is the docblock in the code.

## 6. Adding a file or folder

1. Update this document and `architecture.md` (same activity).
2. Add the test in the documented location.
3. Implement in the documented home.
4. Run the activity gate.

If the file does not fit, the architecture is wrong, not the folder.

## 7. Forbidden

- Generated files inside source directories.
- A second test tree next to the documented one.
- A new top-level folder without a docs update.
- Secrets or environment files in the tree.
